--TEST--
A `get` hook and a block-bodied `fn` answer for a path that reaches their closing brace, exactly as a method does — `rule:types/declaration`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The promise is the declaration's, not the method's: every block body checked
// against a non-`void` type is walked for a path that leaves through the
// bottom. Both bodies below return on one path and fall off the other.
class Reading {
    public int $celsius = 20;

    public int $doubled {
        get {
            if ($this->celsius > 0) {
                return $this->celsius * 2;
            }
        }
    }
}

var $clamp = fn (int $x): int => {
    if ($x > 0) {
        return $x;
    }
};
echo $clamp(1), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0739]: `Reading::$doubled::get` declares `int` but a path reaches the end of its body
%A
error[E0739]: the closure declares `int` but a path reaches the end of its body
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
